## Context

Opened by `merge-gate.py run-after --open-ticket` (ticket 1251): the full
declared set failed on main after a merge.

Tip: 08cd9ec1cab68aa2f809fe49cfb027dd3dfd9110
Failing checks: pytest-guard
Last green after-merge tip: 78ba2235d6450d994d6bd6a5d6a42f4059b8c910
Merges since (first parent, newest first):
- 08cd9ec1cab6 Merge pull request #1957 from MinhHaDuong/t1334-health-checkup

Failed tests (check, test id):
- pytest-guard tests/test_bash_suites.py::test_shell_suite[test_shell_init_gh_agent.sh]

## Scope

`scripts/shell-init.sh` (around line 67) prints the "Disk headroom warning"
on stdout when sourced; `tests/test_shell_init_gh_agent.sh` captures the
sourcing shell's stdout, so any host under 10% free turns the test red.
Disk is back at 12% free and the test passes today: the trap remains.
Send the warning to stderr (an interactive-shell notice belongs there);
check `scripts/on-start-context.sh` uses its own channel and is unaffected.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] shell-init.sh emits the disk warning on stderr, not stdout.
- [ ] The test passes with the warning forced on (e.g. a threshold or reading override, or a stubbed `tmp_report.py`), shown in the PR.
- [ ] An after-merge record on main passes the checks named above.
